source: crates/fauxfield/tests/cli.rs
expression: out
---
Add a Route to a Server file (a running host hot-reloads)

Usage: fauxfield route add [OPTIONS] [SERVER] [METHOD] [PATH]

Arguments:
  [SERVER]  Server (ID, name, or file slug)
  [METHOD]  HTTP method (case-insensitive) or ANY
  [PATH]    Path or pattern (`/users/:id`, `/files/*rest`, or a regex with --match regex)

Options:
  -q, --quiet                Suppress informational output
      --status <STATUS>      Status of the default Response (100-599)
      --body <BODY>          Body of the default Response
      --no-color             Disable coloured output (also honoured: the NO_COLOR environment variable)
      --body-file <FILE>     Read the default Response body from a file
      --from-json <FILE|->   Full Route definition as JSON (same schema as the MCP `upsert_route` tool); `-` reads stdin
      --match <MODE>         Match mode; omitted means inferred and nothing is written [possible values: exact, param, regex]
      --folder <FOLDER>      Folder (ID or unique name)
      --name <NAME>          Route name
      --priority <PRIORITY>  Priority (higher wins; default 0)
  -w, --workspace <PATH>     Workspace folder (default: the nearest ancestor containing fauxfield.toml, else the current directory)
      --json                 Machine-readable output with a stable schema
  -h, --help                 Print help
